  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>L'Esquinade is a beach restaurant on Pampelonne, in Ramatuelle, entering its 54th year according to the tourist office. It stands with its feet in the water, by the sea, and serves mussels, grilled dishes and wood-fired pizzas in a regional cuisine. It seats 200, including 150 on the terrace, and also has a fireplace and baby chairs.</p>

      <h2>With your dog</h2>
      <p>The Ramatuelle tourist office and Golfe de Saint-Tropez Destination (two official sites) both list "Pets welcome" among the restaurant's services; neither specifies any condition (leash, size, area of the terrace or sand). No official contradiction was found. Dogs being allowed at the restaurant says nothing about dog access to the beach itself, which follows the municipality's rules.</p>

      <h2>Hours, prices and access</h2>
      <p>The Ramatuelle tourist office lists opening daily from 14 February 2026 to 10 January 2027, with lunch service, then lunch and dinner from 1 June to 1 October. A second tourist office listing, for the beach restaurant, gives 5 April to 4 October: the periods differ, so a call helps before travelling out of season. À la carte, expect 20 to 35 euros; the children's menu is 13 euros. Cash, bank cards and American Express are accepted. Parking is paid, with parking nearby; the beach is supervised, wifi is available and beach equipment and mattresses can be rented. Phone: 04 94 45 34 89; there is also an Instagram account (@esquinade_plage).</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the terrace seats 150, but Pampelonne is very busy in high season: book by phone and bring fresh water for your dog.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The restaurant is on Pampelonne beach itself, so you can follow the meal with a walk by the water while respecting the municipal rules on dogs in season.</p>
